# Teaching the Scientific Method: It's All in the Perspective

**Authors:** Ayers, James M., Ayers, Kathleen M.

## Abstract
A three unit module of inquiry, including morphological comparison, cladogram construction, and data mining has been developed to teach students the nature of experimental science. Students generate angiosperm morphological data, form cladistic hypotheses, then mine taxonomic, bioinformatic and historical data from many sources to replicate and verify those hypotheses.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ752778

